# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training data
#
# The CSVs are large (22 MB for BRFSS alone) and are inputs, not outputs.
# `python ml_model/train_all.py` needs them; see the README for sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
ml_model/data/

# Superseded local-only scripts, kept on disk for reference but not published.
ml_model/train_all_models.py
ml_model/convert_and_quantize.py

# Internal working notes -- not published. These predate the model rebuild and
# their figures are stale; README.md and app/models/*/metadata.json are current.
ADVANCEMENT_ROADMAP.md
MODEL_IMPROVEMENT_SUMMARY.md
TRAINING_RESULTS.md
PROJECT_REPORT_PROPER.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model artefacts are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The previous version of this file excluded three of the four models because
# they ran to hundreds of megabytes, which meant a fresh clone could not run
# the app at all -- /sleep/ returned a 500 and /heart_disease/ an error page.
# The retrained models total ~0.5 MB and are committed, so
# `git clone && pip install -r requirements.txt && python run.py` just works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
